From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Subject: [PATCH] Pass content type changes on to Qt Virtual Keyboard

Qt Virtual Keyboard reads the input method hints only when it is asked to
update. The content type a newly focused field sends after the input
context is set up was therefore only picked up with the next surrounding
text change, which is the application's response to the first key. The
change of hints at that point resets the input method, so an input method
that composes in the preedit (Korean) lost the first jamo of the first
word: 허망 came out as ㅓ망 in Qt applications.

Ask Qt Virtual Keyboard to update its hints as soon as the content type
arrives.
---
diff --git a/src/inputlisteneritem.cpp b/src/inputlisteneritem.cpp
index ca6bb6a..eb71d5f 100644
--- a/src/inputlisteneritem.cpp
+++ b/src/inputlisteneritem.cpp
@@ -95,6 +95,15 @@ InputListenerItem::InputListenerItem()
             }
         }
     });
+    // Qt Virtual Keyboard only reads the hints in update(). Without this, the
+    // content type of a newly focused field reached it with the first
+    // surrounding text change, i.e. after the first key, and the change of
+    // hints reset the input method in the middle of the first word.
+    connect(&m_input, &InputPlugin::contentTypeChanged, this, [this] {
+        if (m_input.hasContext()) {
+            QGuiApplication::inputMethod()->update(Qt::ImHints);
+        }
+    });
     connect(&m_input, &InputPlugin::deactivate, this, [this] {
         QGuiApplication::inputMethod()->setVisible(false);
         QGuiApplication::inputMethod()->reset();
